  "caption": "Quinn's brain had too many tabs open, evenings were for doom-scrolling, and \"just exercise\" sounded exhausting.\n\nThe research on exercise for low mood and anxiety is encouraging. Consistency tends to matter more than the type or intensity, and benefits can show up within weeks. It works alongside professional care rather than replacing it.\n\nWhat can help: starting tiny with a 10-minute walk, attaching it to a habit like your morning coffee, bringing a buddy or joining a group, getting outdoors where you can, and treating missed days as normal. Mood often lifts before fitness does.\n\nIf distress hangs around, talk to your GP. If pain keeps stopping you from moving, a physio can help you find a way in.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
